.TH MERMAN-CLI-THEME-CHECK 1 2026-08-15 "Merman 0.11.0" "Merman CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
merman\-cli\-theme\-check \- Validate a v2 document and show its contrast results
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmerman\-cli theme check\fR [\fB\-\-appearance\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\-contrast\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-operation\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate a v2 document and show its contrast results
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-appearance\fR \fI<APPEARANCE>\fR
Check this appearance. Defaults to the document\*(Aqs default appearance
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\-contrast\fR
Fail when any checked contrast pair misses its target
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the resolved theme, contrast ratios, and diagnostics as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Theme document JSON file. Use `\-` for stdin
.SH "OPERATION CONTROL"
.TP
\fB\-\-operation\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MILLISECONDS>\fR
Cancel the complete command operation after this many milliseconds.

The deadline starts before input acquisition and covers generation, rendering, and publication. Omit this option for no deadline. Zero cancels at the first cooperative checkpoint. Resource budgets are independent; an unbounded resource profile does not disable this deadline. Blocking backend calls return to a checkpoint before cancellation.
.SH VERSION
v0.11.0
